libvlc: change filters and their options while playing

libVLC 4 has no public way to enable a filter module on a running player:
per-media options (":video-filter=…", ":audio-filter=…") never reach the
player-owned outputs, which are reused across media. VLC's own interface
does this through core APIs (var_SetString on the vout, aout_EnableFilter).

Add two setters following libVLC's existing pattern (value on the player,
so outputs created later inherit it, then on every running output):

- libvlc_media_player_set_filter(): enable or disable a video, subpicture
  or audio filter module by name.
- libvlc_media_player_set_filter_option(): set a filter option, parsed by
  its configured type.

libvlc_media_player_set_equalizer() replaced the whole audio filter chain
with "equalizer"; it now toggles only the equalizer, so other audio filters
stay enabled.

Carried by Ferricone Player on top of VLC a5538c55; written for upstream.

